<title>USA: Coca-Cola Bottling stake upped by Tweedy.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola Bottling stake upped by Tweedy.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Tweedy Browne Co LP said Monday it raised its stake in Coca-Cola Bottling Co Consolidated to 524,020 common shares or 7.44 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 15,100 common bought between February 26 and March 6 at prices ranging from $43.50 to $43.875 per share.</p>
<p>The Charlotte-based firm is the nation's second largest Coca-Cola bottler, with franchise bottling operations across the southeast.</p>
</text>
